e.** She co-sponsored the bill, so this is a `record` / `sponsor`. The `actor_quote` is \"Michalski , Schutt , Penterman\". The `provision_quote` is from section (3)(e): \"(e) The right to determine the names and pronouns used for the child while at\".\n\nBoth passages are `in-term`. She served in the Assembly and is now a candidate for the Senate of the same legislature, which counts under V5 option B.\n\n**Why the chair is blank:**\n- Section (3)(e) points to the parental side, toward rung 5: \"Require parental permission before staff use a different name or pronouns\".\n- But AB 510 lists sixteen unrelated parental rights, covering religion, medical records, surveillance systems and discipline. I coded it `multi-subject`, and I applied that to her sponsorship as well as her vote.\n- None of her own words tie her support to the names-and-pronouns clause. So the bill shows which side she is on, not which rung.\n\n**`needs_source`:**\n- Her own words on telling parents or asking their permission for a student's name or pronoun change at school.\n- Any single-subject Wisconsin bill or amendment on that question that she sponsored or voted on.\n\nNo quotes: the sources hold no words of her own.","ttft_ms":12512,"type":"result","duration_ms":29645,"uuid":"47c50bb1-49f4-4f02-a099-6c2c466e5fc9","ttft_stream_ms":1736,"time_to_request_ms":122,"first_content_frame_ms":1736,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
